  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS. F-COT-LEV-SPX produced CAGR 14.198516%, Sharpe 1.488520 and MDD 8.060422%. It underperformed frozen V11 on both CAGR and Sharpe and also underperformed its availability-matched unconditional retention control (CAGR 14.362971%, Sharpe 1.493322). It beat the matched control in only 3/7 fixed folds. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20,000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=22.770% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=30.010%; both median incremental deltas were negative and candidate MDD P97.5 was 15.065%, slightly above the frozen 15% ceiling. Cumulative 26-trial DSR probability was 91.362%, below 95%. The weekly S&P 500 Consolidated Leveraged Money net-long-share change therefore did not show reliable incremental timing value under the frozen conservative CFTC availability policy. Per the stop rule, no trader-category, Nasdaq-confirmation, positioning-window, threshold, sign, retention-fraction, stale-rule or availability-policy rescue is permitted in this COT campaign.",
